ref 17592186045417] [17592186524508 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a6a586f-0cf2-5116-a740-1a9d8f1242c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524596 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524596 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524596 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88a6fa17-dfc1-5da9-b77a-35d12299dbb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524709 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524709 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524709 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c944dd89-80c1-5096-989e-9c5466682fc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524722 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4y(t)\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524722 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524722 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd2ca45a-40c5-5ab4-aa0e-968f3478e0f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524901 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8d768191-43c2-52ef-8bd4-abb5c4c7e134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1c/1cd11c63564050d5851c53e6a808e6a7b73ee33ce6cbe77c9278c6a3429eaec5.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait for a decoupled system above.\nWhich of the following systems could correspond to the given portrait?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa1fc563-4426-5908-b1bd-3188967331c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525064 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing a decoupled system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are parallel to the axes. These correspond to so-called straight-line solutions of the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The tangents along the $x$-axis are pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\n- The tangents along the $y$-axis are also pointing toward the origin, meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nAmong the options, the only system that satisfies ${\\lambda }_{1}<0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}<0$ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525079 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525079 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f042b9b-5541-5e4f-946e-597ca617d6fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525079 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186305101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525104 #edb/ref 1